  "id": "COMPOUND:38076 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Butyl octanoate is implicated in the biological activity leading to the target of FaDu through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Butyl octanoate acts as a target for multiple compounds, with HCC1937 being a common intermediate in these pathways. HCC1937 is a target of both Maplexin B and Nezukol, and in one pathway, it is also a target of another compound, 3,7-Dimethylocta-1,6-Dien-3-Yl 3-Methylbutanoate. This indicates that Butyl octanoate may influence the biological activity of these compounds, which in turn affect FaDu. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Butyl octanoate could modulate the activity of various targets, ultimately influencing FaDu. The evidence supports a role for Butyl octanoate in the regulation of FaDu through a complex network of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
